	"bugClass": {
		"id": "row-removed-before-acknowledgment",
		"title": "Actionable row disappears before its confirmation is visible",
		"cause": "The view uses membership in the pending list to control the lifetime of a row that also displays the action result. Hiding an answered ID, optimistically removing an item, or replacing the list after a refresh can therefore unmount the row or its enclosing section before the user sees the acknowledged choice and the row finishes its exit.",
		"criteria": "Follow a successful answer or dismissal from the selected state through the next render. Count a match if any one path hides the row or its section too early: an answered-ID check suppresses it, an optimistic update removes it, or a refresh supplies a list that omits it. Check the last item in a section as well as an item with siblings. The deciding evidence is that removal prevents a visible confirmation followed by a completed collapse. A filter or refresh alone is insufficient.",
